   the right to use, modify and distribute it within Fridge+ without compensation.
3. What is forbidden without the publisher's prior written permission: copying, reproducing,
   modifying, adapting, translating, compiling, running in production, distributing, publishing,
   selling, renting, sublicensing, hosting or otherwise exploiting the Code or any part of it,
   as is or modified, and creating derivative works from it.
4. Trademarks and identity. The name "Fridge+", the logo, visuals, texts and visual identity are
   not covered by the reading permission and remain the publisher's exclusive property.
5. Data and services. The Code includes neither the application's data, nor its secrets, nor its
   services (database, payment, e-mail, monitoring). Nothing here grants access to those services
   or to https://fridgeplus.app other than under the website's terms of use.
6. No warranty. The Code is published "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied.
   The publisher shall not be liable for any damage arising from its consultation.
7. Governing law. French law. The French Intellectual Property Code applies unless otherwise agreed.

